---
title: "Payment method"
description: "Manage the payment card on file for your Photon organization."
---

The organization payment method is the card Photon charges. It is separate
from the plans, subscriptions, and usage under
[project billing](/cli/projects/billing). It uses the
[selected organization](/cli/organizations#select-an-organization).

```text
photon org billing payment-method
├── status
└── setup [--no-browser]
```

## Check the card on file

```sh
photon org billing payment-method status
```

```json
{"cardOnFile":true,"paymentMethod":{"brand":"visa","expiresMonth":12,"expiresYear":2028,"last4":"4242"}}
```

With `--json`, the command prints the API's response as Photon sends it.
Photon's API defines that response as card metadata only: `cardOnFile`, and
in `paymentMethod` (which can be `null`) the card's brand, expiry month and
year, and last four digits, with no processor identifiers. Before it prints
a card on file, the CLI checks the brand, last four digits, and expiry, and
fails with `ORGANIZATION_PROTOCOL_ERROR` when they aren't valid card details.
Without `--json`, it shows card details only when `cardOnFile` is true.

## Add or replace a card

`setup` creates a hosted HTTPS checkout and opens it in your browser:

```sh
photon org billing payment-method setup
photon org billing payment-method setup --no-browser
```

With `--json`, it prints the checkout the API returns under `checkout`, and
whether the browser opened it:

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Browser opens">
    ```json
    {"checkout":{"checkoutUrl":"https://..."},"opened":true}
    ```
  </Tab>
  <Tab title="--no-browser">
    ```json
    {"checkout":{"checkoutUrl":"https://..."},"opened":false}
    ```

    You get the same document if the browser fails to launch, so you can open
    the URL yourself.
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

When the browser opens, `Opened secure payment setup in your browser.` still
goes to stderr as text, for the person at the terminal. The checkout URL never
goes to stderr: with `--json`, it's only in the JSON on stdout.

<Warning>
  The checkout URL is a bearer credential for the checkout session: anyone
  who has it can use the session. Text output prints it only when the browser
  doesn't open, but the JSON always holds it, so keep JSON output out of
  shared logs.
</Warning>

Invalid or non-HTTPS checkout URLs are rejected before they are opened or
displayed.

<Note>
  This command replaced `photon account billing payment`, which now only
  points here.
</Note>
